<section class="section" id="discrepancies" aria-labelledby="discrepancies-heading">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">What we observed</p>
    <h2 id="discrepancies-heading">Where the official files and notifications do not agree</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      These came up while joining the files. They are open questions for the Forest Department, not errors we have
      corrected: the maps keep what the files draw and say so. The full list, with sources, is on the
      <a href="/boundaries-and-notifications/#mapping-gaps">boundary page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="discrepancy-grid">
    <article class="discrepancy-card">
      <span class="discrepancy-figure">about {{ stats.not_mapped_notified_km2 | round }} sq km</span>
      <h3>Part of the 2023 reserve has no outline of its own</h3>
      <p>The 21 revenue villages added to the core, the buffer parts of five forest blocks added by compartment or part, Akelgarh, Ambarani-A and the National Chambal piece have no outline of their own in any public file. Shown on the <a href="#data-gaps">data-gaps map</a>.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="discrepancy-card">
      <span class="discrepancy-figure">501 ha</span>
      <h3>The village rows do not add to the printed total</h3>
      <p>The 24 Rawatbhata village rows of the 5 October 2023 order add to 8,695.28 ha; the order prints 8,194.28 ha. The core sub-total is 690.71 sq km by the printed totals and 695.72 by the rows.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="discrepancy-card">
      <span class="discrepancy-figure">about 26 sq km</span>
      <h3>No file separates core from buffer</h3>
      <p>The 2013 split on the zones map uses the park and sanctuary files whole, which counts parts of Jawahar Sagar and Darrah as core and misses the National Chambal core part; the result is approximate.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="discrepancy-card">
      <span class="discrepancy-figure">about 5.4 km</span>
      <h3>The 2020 ESZ is wider than its stated 0–1 km near Rawatbhata</h3>
      <p>There its outer limit is the edge of the Bhainsrorgarh sanctuary file (5.7 km from the Gazette's own reserve coordinates), on a stretch Annexure-I gives zero width "due to Bhainsroadgarh Sanctuary on the other side". The band also crosses forest blocks partly added to the 2023 buffer, so some land may be both ESZ and buffer.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="discrepancy-card">
      <span class="discrepancy-figure">3.51 sq km</span>
      <h3>Jawara Khurd: a hole the Gazette's own list contradicts</h3>
      <p>Neither ESZ file covers the enclave around Jawara (Jaora) Khurd, and the Gazette's map draws the same loop, yet its village list names Jawara Khurd as an ESZ village. The outline keeps the hole until the Department settles it.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="discrepancy-card">
      <span class="discrepancy-figure">27.84 vs about 32 sq km</span>
      <h3>Akelgarh is listed without a part mark</h3>
      <p>The 2023 order adds Akelgarh to the buffer at 27.84 sq km with no part mark; 7.75 sq km of the block has been core since 2013, and the Kota file draws the rest at about 32 sq km. At least about 8 sq km of the addition falls outside the reserve-and-ESZ outline.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="discrepancy-card">
      <span class="discrepancy-figure">6.2 sq km</span>
      <h3>Daulatpura: enclosed by the files, included by none</h3>
      <p>The reserve and Bhainsrorgarh files close round an area near Daulatpura that neither includes; the 2020 ESZ file covers 6.1 sq km of it. The reserve file itself still draws the 2013 reserve although the server copy is dated 24 February 2025.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="discrepancy-card">
      <span class="discrepancy-figure">201.4 / 205.47 / 275.45</span>
      <h3>Three areas for one sanctuary</h3>
      <p>The Bhainsrorgarh sanctuary is 201.4 sq km in its file attribute, 205.47 sq km as the file draws it, 193.09 sq km as the 2023 order's forest blocks add up (by our sum) and 275.45 sq km in the 2021 ESZ notification.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
